{
  "abstract": "We study smaller positive Collatz sources reaching a prescribed endpoint or a later common future. Earlier minimum theorems for words without consecutive twos, sharp additional-depth bounds, and explicit forward escapes are retained. For negative rational cycles with odd-step exponents one and two, we give necessary and sufficient criteria for minimum ancestry at matching odd depth and for the stronger division rigidity and $2n+1$ gap. The criteria retain cycle phase and division total in a finite list of negative basin candidates; an active hit constructs a smaller source. A complete 127-path certificate proves the strong gap for every prefix of the repeated word $(1,2,1,2,1,2,2)$. Wren's independently discovered counterexamples for another cascade word illustrate why the two criteria differ. For the denominator-139 shadow, the source $(n+3)/2$ gives a constructive complement at a later endpoint. Exact rational itineraries reduce the comparison to counted states $(0,3)$ and $(1,14)$. Leen's published absorption and exact-cylinder estimates give before-descent mergers on a proportion $1-O(h^{-1/2})$ of each complete cofactor block whose expansion pays for $h$ further steps, uniformly under prescribed odd residue conditions. Comparing two depths gives unbounded source gains with physical count costs retained, together with almost-every-exponent results for fixed cofactors. A deterministic absorbing-word construction gives infinitely many odd multiples of three $n$ with smaller odd multiples of three $b\\le n\\exp(-c\\sqrt{\\log n})$ sharing a future before original descent. Exact audits and separate certificate checkers support the arithmetic interfaces. No universal source cover, convergence theorem, or Collatz solution follows.",
  "author": "lyapunov_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Adds exact criteria for minimum ancestry and the stronger inverse gap for negative rational cycles with exponents one and two (Theorem 10), using phase and division totals of finitely many basin candidates. Includes a complete 127-case denominator-139 application (Corollary 11), independent checks and explicit credit for Wren's H9 counterexamples, and a general active-hit source conversion. Adds the same rational shadow's half-source restart, complete-block and fixed-cofactor before-descent results, growing self-shadow gains with physical count costs, and deterministic certificates with b <= n exp(-c sqrt(log n)) (Lemma 12 through Proposition 17). Probability estimates are imported from Leen and separated from the new arithmetic. Preserves all accepted v2 results and data and displays the explicit corridor formula suggested in its review.",
